# Deep felt-experience: prescription benzodiazepines.
from gen import D
F={}
def S(k,o,p,pl,c): F[k]={"onset":o,"peak":p,"plateau":pl,"comedown":c}
S("lorazepam",
["Lorazepam (Ativan) is a medium-acting, fairly strong benzodiazepine. Swallowed or dissolved under the tongue, it settles in over a short while: the shoulders drop, the jaw unclenches, a heaviness gathers behind the eyes and the chest loosens as if a tight band has been let out.","Mentally the onset feels like someone turning down the volume on fear. Racing thoughts slow, the 'what if' loop goes quiet, and many people describe a soft, blanketed feeling of safety. It is more sedating and less floaty than alprazolam, and often comes with a pull toward sleep.","Light-headedness and unsteadiness on standing appear early, and reaction time is already slowed even when the person feels only relaxed."],
["At its peak the body feels heavy, warm and loose; limbs are slow to respond, speech may slur slightly, and coordination is clumsy. Many people simply fall asleep.","Mentally the peak is calm, indifferent and foggy. Worries feel distant and unimportant, but so do details: lorazepam is strongly linked to anterograde amnesia, so people often cannot remember conversations or actions from this window, sometimes while appearing normal to others.","With alcohol, opioids or other sedatives the peak can slide into dangerously slowed breathing and unresponsiveness."],
["The plateau lasts several hours of steady, quiet sedation. The body remains slack and drowsy, and balance stays poor, which raises the risk of falls, especially in older people.","Mentally the state is muted and even: little anxiety, little drive and weak short-term memory. Some feel a gentle contentment; others feel blank or dull.","Because it lasts long enough to overlap, repeated doses during the plateau stack up and deepen sedation."],
["The comedown is gradual: heaviness thins into tiredness, a foggy head and sometimes a mild headache.","Emotionally anxiety may creep back, sometimes stronger than before ('rebound anxiety'), along with irritability or a flat mood.","Daily use builds tolerance and dependence within weeks. Stopping suddenly can cause severe anxiety, insomnia, tremor, hallucinations and seizures, so tapering with a prescriber is essential."])
S("chlordiazepoxide",
["Chlordiazepoxide (Librium), the first benzodiazepine, is long-acting and gentle in onset. Swallowed, it builds slowly: a mild loosening in the muscles and a quieting of jitteriness rather than a sudden drop.","Mentally the onset is a soft, gradual calm that people often barely notice until they realize they are no longer tense. It is commonly used for alcohol withdrawal for this reason.","Drowsiness and slight unsteadiness are the earliest side effects."],
["At its peak the body feels relaxed and slightly heavy, with mild clumsiness.","Mentally there is steady calm and reduced worry, with less euphoria than faster benzos.","Combined with alcohol or opioids, breathing and consciousness can be dangerously depressed."],
["Its long-lasting breakdown products keep a mild sedation going for a very long time, sometimes building over days with repeated use. The body feels steady and slow.","Mentally people feel level and dulled, with weakened memory and concentration that may go unnoticed.","Accumulation is a particular risk in older adults, causing confusion and falls."],
["The comedown is very slow and soft, which is why it is used for tapering.","Emotionally anxiety returns gradually rather than suddenly.","Dependence still develops with long use; stopping should be done gradually."])
S("temazepam",
["Temazepam (Restoril) is a medium-short benzodiazepine used for sleep. Swallowed, its onset brings a heaviness in the limbs and eyelids, a warm loosening and an urge to lie down.","Mentally the onset is a drowsy calm that dissolves the restless, wired feeling of insomnia; thoughts get slower and softer.","In the 1990s, liquid-filled capsules were misused by injection in the UK, causing severe vein damage, and were withdrawn."],
["At its peak the body is relaxed and sleepy, coordination poor and speech possibly thick.","Mentally there is a drifting, dreamy calm leading to sleep; people who stay awake can become disinhibited and forgetful.","With alcohol or opioids breathing can be dangerously suppressed."],
["The plateau is a few hours of deep sleep or heavy drowsiness.","Mentally foggy, with patchy memory.","Waking in the night may bring confusion and unsteadiness."],
["Next morning some feel a mild hangover: grogginess, slowed thinking and dry mouth.","Emotionally a slightly flat mood or anxiety may follow.","Nightly use leads to tolerance and rebound insomnia when stopped."])
S("triazolam",
["Triazolam (Halcion) is a very short-acting, potent sleep benzodiazepine. It comes on fast: a sudden heaviness, drooping eyelids and slackening muscles.","Mentally the onset can be abrupt, like a dimmer switch: alertness drops and thoughts blur quickly.","Because it acts so fast, people who do not go straight to bed can find themselves doing things they will not remember."],
["At its peak the body is very sleepy and uncoordinated.","Mentally it causes strong amnesia; unusual behavior, confusion or agitation can occur, especially at higher amounts.","Combined with alcohol it is particularly dangerous."],
["The plateau is short, a few hours.","Mentally sleep or foggy semi-awareness.","Its brief action means the body clears it before morning."],
["The comedown is quick, but some notice early-morning anxiety or wakefulness as it wears off.","Emotionally next-day anxiety ('rebound') has been reported.","Tolerance and dependence develop; stopping should be tapered."])
S("oxazepam",
["Oxazepam (Serax) is a slow-onset, medium-acting benzodiazepine often used for anxiety and alcohol withdrawal. Its onset is gradual and gentle: tension eases over a while without a rush.","Mentally a quiet, even calm builds slowly.","Its slow start makes it less likely to be misused for a 'hit'."],
["At its peak the body is relaxed and mildly drowsy.","Mentally calm and less worried, with little euphoria.","It is processed without the liver's main enzyme pathway, making it safer for people with liver disease."],
["The plateau is several hours of steady calm.","Mentally clear-ish but slowed.","Breathing risk rises with alcohol or opioids."],
["The comedown is soft.","Emotionally anxiety returns gradually.","Dependence develops with long use."])
S("clorazepate",
["Clorazepate (Tranxene) is converted in the stomach to nordazepam, a very long-acting benzodiazepine. Onset is moderately fast: muscles loosen and anxiety settles.","Mentally a steady calm.","Drowsiness appears early."],
["At its peak relaxed and mildly sedated.","Mentally calm and less reactive.","Combining with depressants is dangerous."],
["The plateau is very long as nordazepam lingers for days.","Mentally dulled, with reduced memory and focus.","Accumulation causes confusion in older people."],
["The comedown is extremely gradual.","Emotionally slow return of anxiety.","Dependence develops with long use."])
S("midazolam",
["Midazolam (Versed) is a fast, short benzodiazepine used before procedures and in seizures, by injection, nasal spray or mouth. Onset is very quick: a swift heaviness and relaxation, often within minutes.","Mentally anxiety vanishes almost immediately, replaced by a dreamy, uncaring calm.","Its strong amnesic effect means patients usually remember little of the procedure."],
["At its peak deeply relaxed, drowsy and uncoordinated.","Mentally hazy and forgetful; some patients become talkative or disinhibited.","Breathing can be depressed, especially with opioids, so it is used with monitoring."],
["The plateau is short, under an hour or two.","Mentally drifting and foggy.","Flumazenil can reverse it in emergencies."],
["The comedown is a groggy waking with patchy memory.","Emotionally calm or briefly confused.","Prolonged infusions in intensive care can cause dependence and withdrawal."])
S("flunitrazepam",
["Flunitrazepam (Rohypnol) is a potent sleep benzodiazepine, not sold in the US, notorious for misuse in drug-facilitated assault. Its onset brings heavy, sudden sedation and loss of coordination.","Mentally there is quick confusion and blankness, and strong amnesia.","The manufacturer added a dye so it turns drinks blue, but generics and counterfeits may not."],
["At its peak extreme drowsiness, slurred speech and inability to stand.","Mentally disinhibition or unconsciousness, with little or no memory.","With alcohol it can cause dangerous breathing suppression."],
["The plateau lasts many hours of deep sleep or stupor.","Mentally absent or confused.","Anyone who suspects they were drugged should seek medical help and testing quickly."],
["The comedown brings grogginess, headache and gaps in memory.","Emotionally confusion, fear or distress.","Dependence develops with repeated use."])
S("clobazam",
["Clobazam (Onfi) is a 1,5-benzodiazepine used mainly for epilepsy. Its onset is gradual, with mild relaxation.","Mentally it tends to cause less sedation than other benzos; people feel calmer with clearer thinking.","Drowsiness can still occur."],
["At its peak mild calm and relaxation.","Mentally steady with less euphoria.","Risks rise with alcohol or opioids."],
["The plateau is long, with a long-acting metabolite.","Mentally mostly clear.","Behavior changes and irritability occur in some."],
["The comedown is gradual.","Emotionally steady.","Stopping suddenly can trigger seizures."])
S("etizolam",
["Etizolam is a thienodiazepine prescribed in Japan, India and Italy and sold widely as a research chemical and in counterfeit pills, especially 'street Valium' in Scotland. Its onset is quick: muscles release, the chest eases and a warm drowsiness spreads.","Mentally it feels like a bright, sociable calm, often compared to alprazolam, with anxiety vanishing fast.","Counterfeit products vary in strength and may contain other drugs."],
["At its peak heavy relaxation and clumsiness.","Mentally calm, disinhibited and forgetful.","With opioids it has been involved in many deaths in Scotland."],
["The plateau is a few hours of drowsy calm.","Mentally foggy.","Redosing to maintain the effect is common."],
["The comedown brings rebound anxiety and tiredness.","Emotionally irritable and low.","Dependence develops fast; withdrawal can include seizures."])
# Less common prescription benzodiazepines: drug-specific notes on a shared outline.
def B(k,intro,char,dur,note):
    long_=dur=="long"; short=dur=="short"
    S(k,[intro+" "+("It comes on quickly: muscles loosen, eyelids grow heavy and a warm drowsiness spreads." if short else "It comes on gradually: shoulders drop, the jaw unclenches and a mild heaviness settles into the limbs."),
    "Mentally the onset is "+char+" Worries recede and the mind becomes slower and quieter.",
    "Unsteadiness, slowed reactions and drowsiness start early, even when the person feels only relaxed."],
    ["At its peak the body feels loose and heavy, with clumsiness, sometimes slurred speech and a strong pull toward sleep.","Mentally the peak is calm and detached, with weakened memory for events during this time.","With alcohol, opioids or other sedatives, breathing and consciousness can be dangerously depressed."],
    [("The plateau is very long because the drug and its breakdown products linger for days; with repeated use it builds up." if long_ else "The plateau is short, a few hours, ending before morning when used for sleep." if short else "The plateau lasts several hours of steady sedation.")+" Balance and coordination stay poor.","Mentally people feel muted and dulled, with poor concentration.",note],
    [("The comedown is very gradual, and next-day grogginess is common." if long_ else "The comedown is fairly quick, and some notice rebound anxiety or early waking."),"Emotionally anxiety may creep back with irritability or flatness.","Daily use causes tolerance and dependence; stopping suddenly can cause seizures, so tapering is essential."])
B("flurazepam","Flurazepam (Dalmane) is an older sleep benzodiazepine with a very long-acting metabolite.","heavy and sleepy, less calm-focused than sleep-inducing.","long","Next-day sedation and confusion are common, especially in older adults.")
B("estazolam","Estazolam (ProSom) is a medium-acting triazolo sleep benzodiazepine.","a drowsy, drifting calm that eases into sleep.","medium","Waking during the night can bring confusion.")
B("quazepam","Quazepam (Doral) is a long-acting sleep benzodiazepine.","a slow, heavy drowsiness.","long","Accumulation can cause daytime sleepiness.")
B("remimazolam","Remimazolam (Byfavo) is a new ultra-short intravenous benzodiazepine used for procedural sedation, broken down rapidly in the blood.","a quick, hazy calm that slides into sedation within minutes.","short","It is used only with monitoring, and patients usually recover quickly.")
B("nitrazepam","Nitrazepam (Mogadon) is a long-acting sleep benzodiazepine used in the UK and elsewhere.","a heavy, sleepy calm.","long","Hangover sedation the next day is common.")
B("bromazepam","Bromazepam (Lexotan) is a medium-acting anxiety benzodiazepine popular in Europe.","a clear, relaxed calm with lessened tension.","medium","It can feel less sleepy than diazepam at lower amounts.")
B("lormetazepam","Lormetazepam (Noctamid) is a short-medium sleep benzodiazepine used in Europe.","a soft drowsiness leading into sleep.","short","It is also given by injection in some anesthesia settings.")
B("prazepam","Prazepam (Centrax) is a prodrug converted to nordazepam, so it starts slowly and lasts long.","a slow, steady calm.","long","Its slow onset means little rush.")
B("halazepam","Halazepam (Paxipam) was a long-acting anxiety benzodiazepine, now discontinued in the US.","a gradual, gentle calm.","long","It was converted mostly to nordazepam.")
B("camazepam","Camazepam is a medium-acting benzodiazepine used in some European countries.","a mild, clear calm with less sleepiness.","medium","It is reported to cause less impairment than many benzos.")
B("cloxazolam","Cloxazolam (Sepazon) is a long-acting prodrug benzodiazepine used in Japan and Latin America.","a slow, steady relief of tension.","long","Effects accumulate with repeated use.")
B("delorazepam","Delorazepam (EN) is a long-acting benzodiazepine popular in Italy.","a heavy, lasting calm.","long","Its long action means sedation can stretch into the next day.")
B("ethyl-loflazepate","Ethyl loflazepate (Victan) is a very long-acting benzodiazepine used in France and elsewhere.","a mild, steady calm.","long","It is valued for causing less sleepiness, but accumulation still occurs.")
B("fludiazepam","Fludiazepam (Erispan) is a potent benzodiazepine used in Japan.","a quick, strong easing of anxiety.","medium","Misuse has been reported in Taiwan.")
B("haloxazolam","Haloxazolam (Somelin) is a sleep benzodiazepine used in Japan.","a drowsy, sleep-inducing calm.","long","Next-day drowsiness can occur.")
B("ketazolam","Ketazolam is a long-acting benzodiazepine prodrug used in Spain and elsewhere.","a gradual calm and muscle relaxation.","long","It is converted partly to diazepam and nordazepam.")
B("loprazolam","Loprazolam (Dormonoct) is a medium-acting sleep benzodiazepine.","a soft drowsiness leading to sleep.","medium","Some notice mild morning grogginess.")
B("medazepam","Medazepam (Nobrium) is a long-acting benzodiazepine prodrug.","a mild, steady calm.","long","Its active forms linger for days.")
B("nimetazepam","Nimetazepam (Erimin) is a potent sleep benzodiazepine, widely misused in Malaysia and Southeast Asia.","a fast, heavy drowsiness.","medium","Counterfeit 'Erimin 5' tablets have caused harm.")
B("nordazepam","Nordazepam (Calmday) is the long-acting active metabolite of diazepam and many prodrug benzos.","a slow, even calm.","long","It builds up over days.")
B("oxazolam","Oxazolam (Serenal) is a prodrug benzodiazepine used in Japan.","a gradual relief of tension.","long","It is converted mostly to nordazepam.")
B("pinazepam","Pinazepam (Domar) is a long-acting benzodiazepine used in Italy.","a slow, steady calm.","long","Accumulation causes daytime dullness.")
B("tetrazepam","Tetrazepam (Myolastan) was used mainly as a muscle relaxant until withdrawn in Europe in 2013 after serious skin reactions.","a loosening of tight muscles with mild calm.","medium","Severe skin reactions led to its withdrawal.")
B("brotizolam","Brotizolam (Lendormin) is a short-acting thienotriazolo sleep drug used in Europe and Japan.","a fast drowsiness that drops into sleep.","short","Rebound wakefulness can follow.")
B("cinolazepam","Cinolazepam (Gerodorm) is a sleep benzodiazepine used in Austria.","a drowsy calm.","medium","Next-day effects are usually mild.")
B("mexazolam","Mexazolam (Melex) is an anxiety benzodiazepine used in Japan and Portugal.","a mild easing of anxiety.","long","Its metabolites last a long time.")
B("clotiazepam","Clotiazepam (Rize) is a short-acting thienodiazepine for anxiety.","a quick, light calm.","short","It wears off relatively fast.")
B("gidazepam","Gidazepam is a prodrug benzodiazepine used in Russia and Ukraine.","a slow, gentle calm with less sleepiness.","long","Its active metabolite lingers.")
B("tofisopam","Tofisopam (Grandaxin) is an atypical 2,3-benzodiazepine that does not act on the usual benzodiazepine site.","a mild calm with little sedation or muscle relaxation.","short","Unlike typical benzos it causes little sedation or dependence.")
B("bentazepam","Bentazepam is a thienodiazepine used in Spain.","a moderate calm.","medium","Rare liver injury has been reported.")
B("zolazepam","Zolazepam is a veterinary benzodiazepine sold with tiletamine (Telazol) for animal anesthesia.","rapid, deep sedation.","medium","Human exposure is accidental and mixed with the dissociative tiletamine.")
for k,v in F.items():
    if k in D: D[k]["feel"]=v
